# Enables claude-sudo's descriptive password prompt.
#
# Without this, PAM supplies its own bare "Password:" prompt and sudo's -p text
# (the command + justification that claude-sudo builds) is never shown. With it,
# sudo's -p prompt wins.
#
# Install on each machine:
#   sudo cp passprompt_override.example /etc/sudoers.d/passprompt_override
#   sudo chmod 440 /etc/sudoers.d/passprompt_override
#   sudo visudo -cf /etc/sudoers.d/passprompt_override   # verify
#
# The target name must have no dot in it - sudo ignores files in
# /etc/sudoers.d/ whose names contain "." - so it is NOT named *.example there.

Defaults passprompt_override
